From: limina <gustavo@noronha.eti.br>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: advertise DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR on planes (limina direct scanout)

virtio-gpu sets fb_modifiers_not_supported and passes no modifier list to
plane init, so the planes carry no IN_FORMATS property and ADDFB2 with the
DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS flag is rejected outright. Compositors gate direct
scanout of client dmabufs on exactly that: mutter's crtc_supports_modifier()
requires the buffer's explicit modifier (LINEAR for every buffer on this
device) to be enumerated by the primary plane, so fullscreen direct scanout
can never engage even though the layouts are trivially compatible.

The device's only layout IS linear. Say so: advertise
{DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR} via the plane modifier list (the core then creates
IN_FORMATS) and drop fb_modifiers_not_supported so a LINEAR-tagged ADDFB2
is accepted. No behavioral change for legacy (modifier-less) framebuffers.

Two-tier note: limina enhanced-tier kernel; a stock kernel keeps composited
fullscreen (correct, just more guest GPU/CPU work).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -38,6 +38,11 @@
 	DRM_FORMAT_HOST_ARGB8888,
 };

+static const uint64_t virtio_gpu_format_modifiers[] = {
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
+	DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID
+};
+
 uint32_t virtio_gpu_translate_format(uint32_t drm_fourcc)
 {
 	uint32_t format;
@@ -402,7 +407,8 @@

 	plane = drmm_universal_plane_alloc(dev, struct drm_plane, dev,
 					   1 << index, &virtio_gpu_plane_funcs,
-					   formats, nformats, NULL, type, NULL);
+					   formats, nformats,
+					   virtio_gpu_format_modifiers, type, NULL);
 	if (IS_ERR(plane))
 		return plane;

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c
@@ -350,8 +350,6 @@
 	vgdev->ddev->mode_config.max_width = XRES_MAX;
 	vgdev->ddev->mode_config.max_height = YRES_MAX;

-	vgdev->ddev->mode_config.fb_modifiers_not_supported = true;
-
 	for (i = 0 ; i < vgdev->num_scanouts; ++i)
 		vgdev_output_init(vgdev, i);

